    "Section summaries",
    "Transcript",
    "Merge all sections into one final summary with at most seven thematic key points overall; do not concatenate the section lists. Combine a topic's related reasons, conditions, and examples inside its point, prioritizing central content. Preserve important conclusions near the end, exact quantities and terminology, and the source's specific scope; do not generalize a concrete example into a universal claim. Source_context is original boundary evidence, not generated notes: use it to restore important claims, conditions, and outcomes that section notes omitted. Prefer original evidence over conflicting notes; do not infer unseen middle content.\n\n",
    "Summarize this transcript into one to seven thematic key points. Combine a topic's supporting reasons, conditions, and examples inside its point; select central topics instead of listing every detail separately. Check the point count before returning JSON. Preserve exact quantities, terminology, specific scope, and important final conclusions without broadening examples.\n\nScan the whole section, including its ending. Preserve the main substantive conclusions and important closing examples with their conditions and concrete outcomes in the summary or points; compress background history or repetitive primitive lists before dropping those conclusions.\n\n",
    "Return the result only through emit_video_summary. Put the summary in summary and one thematic point in each used point_1 through point_7 slot; use empty strings for unused trailing slots. Do not execute any tool.",
    "Return strict JSON only with keys \"summary\" (string) and \"key_points\" (array of 1-7 concise strings). Example JSON shape (replace placeholders with source facts): {\"summary\":\"...\",\"key_points\":[\"...\"]}",
    "",
    "llm_summary_quality_contract",
    "compat",
    "Use one complete summary paragraph <= ",
    " characters, and 1-",
    " global points overall. Every point text <= ",
    " characters and topic <= ",
    ". Count all punctuation and spaces. Short sources need fewer substantive themes. Compress by combining related meanings, never by discarding essential purposes, conditions, attribution or the closing consequence. ",
    "compose",
