    "compact",
    "Output statements have exactly text and fact_ids (nonempty arrays of provided fact IDs); points additionally have topic. Summary is 1-",
    " such statements, with at most ",
    " points overall, not per part. Total summary text <= ",
    " characters. Each final point <= ",
    " characters including punctuation and spaces. Every point adds at least one fact ID not used by earlier points; shared context refs are allowed alongside a new fact. Summary may reuse point references. Merge one topic's principle, reason, condition and important example into one compact point; do not make a final leftover catalog. Cover all core fact IDs somewhere in summary or points collectively. Preserve essential conditions, attribution and example scope while removing repetition and low priority material. Do not confuse fact ID coverage with source entailment: check the text itself. Cover a compound core fact's necessary clauses in final summary and points together, not just its topic: actions, purpose, enabling conditions, alternatives and consequences. Support facts can also carry necessary explanations of the main practice. Synthesize the central message in a concise paragraph; short sources need fewer points. Use one point per substantive theme, combining its preparation, reasons and conditions. Keep necessary outline context in summary; do not pad slots with announced topic counts. ",
    "compose",
