    "llm_unconfigured",
    "事实总结质量协议配置无效",
    "Return summary as a paragraph string, point_1 through point_k, and theme_plan. Each point has topic,text,fact_ids. theme_plan has the corresponding contiguous theme_1 through theme_k, each exactly topic,principle,conditions,consequences,fact_ids. Plan all parts together first, then write one point per theme. A fact ID has one primary theme owner; overview facts already carried by summary need not create another point. fact_ids are ownership/association hints, not final citations; the caller derives actual references. Use only provided IDs, never guess. Unused trailing slots may be omitted/null. Do not emit key_points as a second representation. Theme metadata is not proof of support.",
    "This is the planned source-aware audit and final revision. Read all sources including their endings, check every final statement and coverage in both directions. Correct quality_issues and unsupported wording; merge related principles/conditions/examples rather than adding a leftover catalogue. Reallocate themes across all parts if the draft spends slots on the front. Return exactly additional_facts and output. additional_facts is an array, empty if no essential fact is missing; additions have source_id and the given fact fields and use real bracketed line numbers, at most ",
    " additions. Their IDs are A1,A2,... in order. output contains summary as ONE object with text and assertions, and finite point_1 through point_k (k <= ",
    "), each with topic,text,fact_ids,assertions. Each point's fact_ids declares its primary theme ownership; do not assign one primary fact to several points. Summary may carry overview and share references. The caller derives citations, so fact_ids are hints and cannot prove a claim. assertions has exactly four JSON booleans: supported,qualifiers_preserved,attribution_preserved,scope_preserved. Evaluate all four against the original sources for that text. False must remain false when unable to verify; revise text before asserting true. Do not manufacture approval. Do not output a separate checks array or S/P item IDs: the caller maps assertions to its own IDs. Unused trailing point slots may be omitted/null. Shape: {\"additional_facts\":[],\"output\":{\"summary\":{\"text\":\"...\",\"assertions\":{\"supported\":true,\"qualifiers_preserved\":true,\"attribution_preserved\":true,\"scope_preserved\":true}},\"point_1\":{\"topic\":\"...\",\"text\":\"...\",\"fact_ids\":[\"provided-ID\"],\"assertions\":{\"supported\":true,\"qualifiers_preserved\":true,\"attribution_preserved\":true,\"scope_preserved\":true}}}}. This shape is an example, not permission to copy true without checking.",
    "At most ",
    " line numbers per evidence; claim <= ",
    "; topic <= ",
    "; attribution <= ",
    ". ",
    "This is the single planned audit and revision stage. theme_plan is the draft allocation, not proof of coverage; correct or merge themes when the sources require it. Read every source part including its ending, compare each candidate statement against the original source, and return a corrected final output. Check source-to-output coverage too: compare facts' necessary clauses against final text, even for referenced IDs. Restore essential omissions from existing facts without duplicating them. missing_core_fact_ids lists core IDs absent from candidate references. It detects reference gaps only; empty is not semantic proof. Restore their meanings and cite them, not IDs alone. Correct unsupported wording, attribution, frequency/modality, conditional claims, overbroad examples, missing core conclusions, topic repetition, overlong summaries and overlong points. Merge same-theme principles and elaborations despite distinct IDs, retaining necessary meanings. Merge excessive draft summary statements into the final statement limit. Do not merely approve the candidate. Additional_facts may be empty; if an essential source fact was missed, add it with source_id and the same fact fields, using the bracketed line numbers from that source_id's numbered text for evidence. Their IDs will be A1, A2, ... in array order; output may reference these IDs and existing IDs. Add at most ",
    " additional facts in total across all source parts. All core originals and additions must be covered. Output exactly {\"additional_facts\":[],\"output\":{\"summary\":[{\"text\":\"...\",\"fact_ids\":[\"provided-ID\"]}],\"key_points\":[{\"topic\":\"...\",\"text\":\"...\",\"fact_ids\":[\"provided-ID\"]}]},\"checks\":[{\"item_id\":\"S1\",\"supported\":true,\"qualifiers_preserved\":true,\"attribution_preserved\":true,\"scope_preserved\":true}]}. S1, S2, ... identify final summary statements; P1, P2, ... identify final key points. Return exactly one check per final statement and point. Flags must be actual JSON booleans; a false flag reports inability to verify and stops output, so revise before marking it true. The checks are your judgments, not external guarantees.",
