    "compact",
    "In this response, allocate at most ",
    " global themes across all parts before writing points. Combine related principles, reasons, conditions, examples and closing consequences across source parts; do not allocate one slot per fact or part. Each theme has exactly topic, principle, conditions, consequences, fact_ids. Topic <= ",
    "; principle <= ",
    " characters. Conditions and consequences are arrays of 0-",
    " nonempty strings, each <= ",
    " characters. fact_ids may provide known IDs as hints; the caller associates references from text, so do not guess IDs. Return summary and key_points, optionally theme_plan with theme_1 etc. Summary may be a paragraph string or an array of text objects. Each point has topic and text, with optional fact_ids hints; each theme has topic, principle, conditions, consequences and fact_ids. Unused trailing point and theme slots may be omitted or set to null. Nonempty themes correspond in order to nonempty points with the same prefix length. Each theme suggests source facts for its corresponding point. Shared context is allowed alongside new point meaning. Fixed point_i slots are also accepted as a contiguous prefix, up to point_",
